  "description": "Z4 P2 (RFC 9449 §7) — Resource Server side DPoP-bound access-token validator.\n      Validates the inbound `Authorization: DPoP <token>` header together with a fresh\n      DPoP proof, checking:\n        • the proof is structurally valid (htm, htu, iat, jti, signature, embedded JWK),\n        • the proof's `ath` claim equals base64url(SHA-256(access_token)),\n        • the proof's JWK thumbprint matches the access-token's `cnf.jkt` confirmation claim.\n      Issuer-side leg (token endpoint, /authorize binding, replay-store, server-issued nonce\n      challenge) lives in redb.Identity.Core.",
  "id": "redb.Identity.Resource.Dpop",
